When the tip of the fin is insulated
Fins are never insulated because the purpose of the fin is to increase the heat transfer. Here
insulated tip is taken as the heat transfer from the fin tip is negligible compared to large width
surface area, this condition is used to obtain boundary conditions which can be used for
mathematical ease.
