Fin performance
We know that along the length of the fin, temperature decreases and hence the temperature
difference between fin and surrounding decreases along the length and hence heat transfer
decreases along the length of the fin.
Heat transfer from fin will be maximum, when the entire fin is maintained at the base temperature.
The efficiency of a fin is defined as the ratio of actual heat transfer to the maximum heat transfer,
when the entire fin assumed at the base temperature.
