Significance of NTU
For a given overall heat transfer coefficient and for a given fluid, NTU depends on surface area A,
greater the NTU, larger is the surface area i.e., larger is the size of the Heat exchanger. Therefore,
NTU is the measure of size of the heat exchanger.
Note
Baffles are used in the heat exchanger to
1. Support tubes
2. Alter the flow direction
3. Increase turbulence and thereby increasing the heat transfer.
