Types of reflection
1. Specular âŸ¶ Incident angle is equal to Reflected angle.
2. Directional âŸ¶Reflected angle depends on the incident angle.
3. Diffuse âŸ¶Reflected angle is independent of incident angle.
A surface is said to be diffuse surface, when the radiation properties are independent if direction.
Grey surface
A surface is said to be gray surface if radiation properties are independent of wavelength.
