Thermal contact Resistance
When 2 metals surfaces are brought in contact, the contact may
not be perfect due to surface roughness and hence the gap is
filled with air or gas which offers high thermal resistance, due
to lower thermal conductivity. This is known as thermal
contact resistance, because of this resistance, the temperature
profile is not continuous and hence there is a significant
temperature drop at contacting surface.
