Lumped systemAnalysis
Itâ€™s such an analysis in which the temperature varies only with time. But not with space.
Example: - A hot copper ball taken out from oven.
Temperature is a function of time â†’ Lumped system Analysis.
Note: - For lumped system analysis, the conductivity must be high and the object must be small.
